{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '46j|D728|CH[12]|G24|G2x2|R1sc|R1bx4|\"'^def |scenario|changed'\"' DESIGN.md calc_check.py gate.py render_v13.py judging-v13-draft.txt REQUEST-AUDIT.md\"","aggregated_output":"REQUEST-AUDIT.md:15:| L4 \"State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share)\" | \"Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast per scenario\" | D260 clause (3), made family-wide; C3, C4 |\nREQUEST-AUDIT.md:22:| L11 changed | kept | PRD 06 |\nREQUEST-AUDIT.md:64:- `Shared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: <population, measure, scope, period> …`\nREQUEST-AUDIT.md:69:## Earlier forecasts (D728, superseding the note below)\nREQUEST-AUDIT.md:72:the themes in force, \"as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\"\nREQUEST-AUDIT.md:73:The `changed` bullet and the answer fields `changed` and `why_changed` are removed, and code derives them. The schema offers no `prior`\njudging-v13-draft.txt:3:- Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\njudging-v13-draft.txt:4:- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast per scenario. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\nrender_v13.py:19:def nullable(schema):\nrender_v13.py:23:def obj(props, desc=None):\nrender_v13.py:30:def v13_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\nrender_v13.py:37:        'scenario': S,\nrender_v13.py:77:def parts(user):\nrender_v13.py:85:def render(archive_path, calls, family):\nrender_v13.py:102:    user = ('[Family] members:\\n' + '\\n\\n'.join(heads) + f'\\n\\nRelations: {rel}.\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: {shared}.\\n\\n'\nrender_v13.py:104:            + '\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.')   # D728: no earlier forecast\nrender_v13.py:108:def strict(calc, schema):\nrender_v13.py:114:        f['scenario'] = f['scenario'] or 'base'\nrender_v13.py:127:def without_nulls(calc):\nrender_v13.py:138:def main():\ngate.py:18:def store_passages(draw, ids):\ngate.py:25:def packet_passages(ids):\ngate.py:30:def W(population, measure, scope, period):\ngate.py:34:def src(fid, evidence, expression, value, unit, basis, what, component='value', bound=None):\ngate.py:42:def comp(fid, op, inputs, value, unit, what, basis='forecast', **extra):\ngate.py:49:def est(fid, value, unit, what, basis_text, rests_on=(), basis='forecast', **extra):\ngate.py:56:def ans(view_id, outcome, rung, reference):\ngate.py:58:            'pushes': [], 'theme_pushes': [], 'changed': True, 'why_changed': 'w'}\ngate.py:73:def r1_common():\ngate.py:93:def r1(variant):\ngate.py:128:def r2():\ngate.py:149:def r3(variant):\ngate.py:182:def r4():\ngate.py:201:def q01_figs():\ngate.py:217:def g1():\ngate.py:222:def g2():\ngate.py:223:    \"\"\"q01 and q02 with paired scenarios [46g.3]: low and high paths for the company total and the segment, each final range an estimate.\"\"\"\ngate.py:226:            ['i295', 'i106', 'i219', 'i216', 'i288'], scenario='low'),\ngate.py:228:            ['i295', 'i106', 'i219', 'i216', 'i288'], scenario='high'),\ngate.py:229:        comp('gfylo', 'sum', ['gh1', 'gh2lo'], 400.6, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), relation='time_aggregation', scenario='low'),\ngate.py:230:        comp('gfyhi', 'sum', ['gh1', 'gh2hi'], 434.6, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), relation='time_aggregation', scenario='high'),\ngate.py:231:        est('gfy', (400.0, 435.0), 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'the two paths, rounded', ['gfylo', 'gfyhi'], scenario='range'),\ngate.py:234:        est('gshlo', 92.0, '%', W('NVIDIA', 'Data Center share', CO, 'FY2027'), 'the Q1 mix, held', ['gmix'], scenario='low'),\ngate.py:235:        est('gshhi', 93.0, '%', W('NVIDIA', 'Data Center share', CO, 'FY2027'), 'the Q1 mix, a point higher', ['gmix'], scenario='high'),\ngate.py:236:        comp('gdclo', 'share', ['gfylo', 'gshlo'], 368.55, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), scenario='low'),\ngate.py:237:        comp('gdchi', 'share', ['gfyhi', 'gshhi'], 404.18, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), scenario='high'),\ngate.py:239:            ['gdclo', 'gdchi', 'i106'], scenario='range'),\ngate.py:247:def g3():\ngate.py:261:def g4():\ngate.py:275:def codes(result):\ngate.py:282:def run():\ngate.py:332:    item('G2x', f2, G_PASSAGES, g2x, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']), 'C4: scenarios crossed'), '')\ngate.py:335:                              scenario='alt'))\ngate.py:337:    item('R1bx', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\ngate.py:338:                                                         'C4: the base reads an alternate scenario'), '')\ngate.py:341:                               scenario='alt'))\ngate.py:342:    r1x2['figures'].append(comp('altdc', 'share', ['altq3', 'mix'], 99.9, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q3 interim'), scenario='alt'))\ngate.py:345:                            'basis_text': 'unchanged', 'rests_on': [], 'value': 1.0})\ngate.py:346:    item('R1bx2', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x2, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\ngate.py:350:                                scenario='alt'))\ngate.py:352:    item('R1bx4', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x4, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\ngate.py:355:    r1x3['figures'].append(est('altq3', 108.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide as a point', ['g3'], scenario='range'))\ngate.py:365:    r1sc = r1('a')                                    # [46j.1] the company in base, Data Center in alt: the stored contradiction relabelled\ngate.py:368:            f['scenario'] = 'alt'\ngate.py:371:    item('R1sc', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1sc, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'cover' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\ngate.py:372:                                                         'C4: part and whole in different scenarios'), '')\ngate.py:373:    g2x2 = copy.deepcopy(c2)                          # [46j.1] crossing the non-shared share estimates\ngate.py:376:    item('G2x2', f2, G_PASSAGES, g2x2, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\ngate.py:381:    c24 = copy.deepcopy(c2)                           # [46j.2] q22 on q01's published range, per scenario\ngate.py:384:        comp('g28lo', 'apply_growth', ['gfylo', 'g41'], 564.85, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2028'), scenario='low'),\ngate.py:385:        comp('g28hi', 'apply_growth', ['gfyhi', 'g41'], 612.79, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2028'), scenario='high'),\ngate.py:387:            ['g28lo', 'g28hi', 'i256', 'i173'], scenario='range'),\ngate.py:390:    item('G24', f24, G_PASSAGES, c24, lambda r: (not r['errors'], \"passes: q22 per scenario on q01's range\"), '')\ngate.py:395:    ch1 = cc.changed(dict(prev, outcome=418.4), calc_c['answers'][0], figs_c)\ngate.py:396:    ch2 = cc.changed(dict(prev, rung=3, outcome=387.0), calc_c['answers'][0], figs_c)\ngate.py:397:    rows.append(('CH1', ch1[0] is False, f'unchanged: {ch1[1]}', {'errors': [], 'recorded': []}))\ngate.py:398:    rows.append(('CH2', ch2[0] is True and 'rung 3 to 2' in ch2[1], f'changed: {ch2[1]}', {'errors': [], 'recorded': []}))\ngate.py:454:    u1['answers'][1] = {'view_id': 'v9', 'shape': 'unresolved', 'why': 'the segment mix after Q2 is not stated', 'cites': [], 'changed': True,\ngate.py:455:                        'why_changed': 'w'}\ngate.py:465:def main():\nDESIGN.md:1:# judging-v13: related number questions judged together, with a checked calculation (design v10, after council round 46j and D728; for round 46k)\nDESIGN.md:4:the ordinary launchers refuse it (D359, D723). The frozen judge (judging-v7, poc-v118) is unchanged.\nDESIGN.md:22:| Previous conclusion | rung and reasons, cut at 800 characters, unmarked | **not shown** (D728). Whether a member's conclusion changed is derived by code afterwards from its earlier rung, outcome and source figures (`calc_check.changed`) |\nDESIGN.md:33:             scenario: \"base\" | \"<named>\",                       # default \"base\" [46.1]\nDESIGN.md:48:             reasons, cites, pushes, theme_pushes, changed, why_changed }\nDESIGN.md:49:         | { view_id, shape: \"unresolved\", why, cites, changed, why_changed } ]       # no outcome, no rung\nDESIGN.md:61:- **Scenarios carry ranges** [46b.1]. A forecast node is a point within a scenario. A range across members is written as paired\nDESIGN.md:62:  scenarios (for example `low`, `high`) whose nodes stay paired. The analyst's final answer may be a range `estimate` resting on the\nDESIGN.md:63:  scenario outcomes.\nDESIGN.md:73:| **C3 part within whole** [46b.1] | for each declared `part_of`, in each scenario, for each declared period: the part's value, found by walking the graph from the part member's outcome to its node for that period, is at most the whole's. Annual and quarters are compared where the declaration names them | a segment quarter above the company quarter |\nDESIGN.md:74:| **C4 one forecast per shared quantity** [46b.1, 46c.1] | for each shared quantity and period the declaration names, each scenario has exactly one `basis: forecast` node. **Every path** in the graph from a member's outcome to any figure that measures that quantity and period passes through that node. A guide, consensus or other source of a future period may feed the forecast node; no path from an outcome may reach it while avoiding the node | the $108B guide feeding v14's $113.5B forecast and, on another path, v9's Data Center Q3 directly: the same guide node, a bypass |\nDESIGN.md:80:| **C4 scenarios** [46g.3, 46h.1, 46i.1] | each scenario has one forecast node per shared quantity. Scenario membership is derived along the whole path: no figure of a point scenario may depend, at any depth, on a forecast node of another scenario. A `range` summary is an estimate with low and high, is an answer's outcome, and feeds no figure; only it may rest on several scenarios; a bypass is a path that reaches the quantity through no forecast node of any scenario | a low path on the high total; a guide relabelled as an alternate scenario and read by the base |\nDESIGN.md:81:| **C4 derived scenarios** [46j.1] | a figure's scenarios are those of the estimates it rests on at any depth; a point-scenario figure may rest on no estimate of another scenario; related members (`part_of`) cover the same scenarios, so C3 compares like with like | the company in `base` and Data Center in `alt`; crossed share estimates |\nDESIGN.md:83:| **C9 same base** [46f.3, 46j.2] | for each `same_base(later, earlier)`, the later member rests on the earlier member's forecast nodes (its outcome, or the scenario paths behind its range summary), and every path to a figure of the earlier quantity and period passes through one of them; scenarios match by C4 | FY2028 grown from the $392B consensus instead of q01's $400–435B forecast |\nDESIGN.md:98:**The model keeps:** drivers, weights, discounts, scenarios, the choice among overlapping bands, and whether to step off the\nDESIGN.md:114:- v7's request bytes are unchanged (the frozen pins).\nDESIGN.md:149:- **The audit:** every changed sentence is shown with its source (D260, D263, D725, this design), read against a stored family\ncalc_check.py:35:def _num(text):\ncalc_check.py:39:def _scale(unit):\ncalc_check.py:43:def extract(text):\ncalc_check.py:72:def _same(a, b):\ncalc_check.py:76:def _source_errors(fig, passages):\ncalc_check.py:103:def _interval(fig):\ncalc_check.py:109:def _compute(op, inputs, signs, out_unit=None):\ncalc_check.py:148:def _bound_direction(op, ins):\ncalc_check.py:161:def _close(declared, expected, unit):\ncalc_check.py:169:def _quarters(period):\ncalc_check.py:179:def _key(what):\ncalc_check.py:183:def check(family, passages, calc):\ncalc_check.py:351:    # [46j.1] scenario membership derived from the estimates a figure rests on; related members cover the same scenarios\ncalc_check.py:353:        return figs[fid].get('scenario', 'base')\ncalc_check.py:358:        sc = f.get('scenario', 'base')\ncalc_check.py:363:            errors.append(('C4', f'{f[\"id\"]} ({sc}) rests on estimates of another scenario ({\", \".join(sorted(other))})'