{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba calc_check.py | sed -n '185,230p;310,500p'; nl -ba gate.py | sed -n '275,424p'\"","aggregated_output":"   185\t    figs = {}\n   186\t    for fig in calc['figures']:\n   187\t        if fig['id'] in figs:\n   188\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]} is defined twice'))\n   189\t        figs[fig['id']] = fig\n   190\t\n   191\t    def refs(fig):\n   192\t        out = list(fig.get('inputs', []))\n   193\t        out += [r for r in fig.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs or r not in passages]\n   194\t        if fig.get('adjusts'):\n   195\t            out.append(fig['adjusts']['figure'])\n   196\t        if fig.get('bridge'):\n   197\t            out.append(fig['bridge'])\n   198\t        return out\n   199\t\n   200\t    # C7 structure: kinds, operations, dangling, cycles\n   201\t    for fig in figs.values():\n   202\t        if fig.get('kind') not in KINDS or fig.get('basis') not in BASES:\n   203\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: kind {fig.get(\"kind\")} or basis {fig.get(\"basis\")} outside the closed set'))\n   204\t        if fig.get('kind') == 'computed' and fig.get('operation') not in OPERATIONS:\n   205\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: operation {fig.get(\"operation\")} outside the closed set'))\n   206\t        for r in refs(fig):\n   207\t            if r not in figs:\n   208\t                errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]} refers to {r}, which is not defined'))\n   209\t    state = {}\n   210\t\n   211\t    def cyclic(fid):\n   212\t        if state.get(fid) == 1:\n   213\t            return True\n   214\t        if state.get(fid) == 2 or fid not in figs:\n   215\t            return False\n   216\t        state[fid] = 1\n   217\t        hit = any(cyclic(r) for r in refs(figs[fid]))\n   218\t        state[fid] = 2\n   219\t        return hit\n   220\t    if any(cyclic(fid) for fid in figs):\n   221\t        errors.append(('C7', 'the figure graph has a cycle'))\n   222\t        return {'errors': errors, 'recorded': recorded}\n   223\t\n   224\t    # C1 sources, prior pointers\n   225\t    for fig in figs.values():\n   226\t        if fig['kind'] == 'source':\n   227\t            errors += _source_errors(fig, passages)\n   228\t        if fig['kind'] == 'prior' and not fig.get('pointer'):\n   229\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: a prior forecast needs an exact pointer to an earlier answer shown in the request'))\n   230\t\n   310\t    # answers: C7 coverage and ownership, C6 rung, C5 reference\n   311\t    members = family['members']\n   312\t    seen = {}\n   313\t    for ans in calc['answers']:\n   314\t        seen[ans['view_id']] = seen.get(ans['view_id'], 0) + 1\n   315\t    for view_id in members:\n   316\t        if seen.get(view_id, 0) != 1:\n   317\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{view_id} has {seen.get(view_id, 0)} answers; exactly one is required'))\n   318\t    for view_id in seen:\n   319\t        if view_id not in members:\n   320\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{view_id} is not a member of the family'))\n   321\t    outcomes = {}\n   322\t    for ans in calc['answers']:\n   323\t        member = members.get(ans['view_id'])\n   324\t        if member is None:\n   325\t            continue\n   326\t        if ans.get('shape') == 'unresolved':\n   327\t            if 'outcome' in ans or 'rung' in ans or not ans.get('why'):\n   328\t                errors.append(('C7', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: an unresolved answer has a reason and neither outcome nor rung'))\n   329\t            continue\n   330\t        out = figs.get(ans.get('outcome'))\n   331\t        if out is None:\n   332\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: outcome {ans.get(\"outcome\")} is not a figure'))\n   333\t            continue\n   334\t        if _key(out['what']) != _key(member['what']):\n   335\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: outcome {out[\"id\"]} measures {_key(out[\"what\"])}, not the question\\'s {_key(member[\"what\"])}'))\n   336\t        outcomes[ans['view_id']] = out['id']\n   337\t        lo, hi = _interval(out)\n   338\t        band = member['bands'][ans['rung'] - 1]\n   339\t        b_lo, b_hi = band[0] if band[0] is not None else float('-inf'), band[1] if band[1] is not None else float('inf')\n   340\t        if not (lo < b_hi and hi >= b_lo):\n   341\t            errors.append(('C6', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: rung {ans[\"rung\"]} ({band}) contains no part of its outcome {lo}–{hi}'))\n   342\t        ref = ans.get('reference') or {}\n   343\t        if ('figure' in ref) == ('unavailable' in ref):          # [46g.2] exactly one choice\n   344\t            errors.append(('C5', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: the reference must name exactly one of a figure or unavailable'))\n   345\t        elif 'unavailable' in ref:\n   346\t            if not ref['unavailable']:\n   347\t                errors.append(('C5', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: an unavailable reference needs a reason'))\n   348\t        else:\n   349\t            errors += _reference_errors(ans['view_id'], figs.get(ref.get('figure')), figs, passages, refs)\n   350\t\n   351\t    # [46j.1] scenario membership derived from the estimates a figure rests on; related members cover the same scenarios\n   352\t    def scen(fid):\n   353\t        return figs[fid].get('scenario', 'base')\n   354\t\n   355\t    def derived(fid):\n   356\t        return {scen(g) for g in _upstream_of(fid, figs, refs) | {fid} if figs[g]['kind'] == 'estimate' and scen(g) != 'range'}\n   357\t    for f in figs.values():\n   358\t        sc = f.get('scenario', 'base')\n   359\t        if sc == 'range' or f['kind'] not in ('computed', 'estimate'):\n   360\t            continue\n   361\t        other = derived(f['id']) - {sc}\n   362\t        if other:\n   363\t            errors.append(('C4', f'{f[\"id\"]} ({sc}) rests on estimates of another scenario ({\", \".join(sorted(other))})'))\n   364\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n   365\t        if rel['type'] == 'part_of' and rel['part'] in outcomes and rel['whole'] in outcomes:\n   366\t            sp, sw = derived(outcomes[rel['part']]), derived(outcomes[rel['whole']])\n   367\t            if sp != sw:\n   368\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{rel[\"part\"]} covers scenarios {sorted(sp)} but {rel[\"whole\"]} covers {sorted(sw)}; related members cover the same'))\n   369\t\n   370\t    # [46i.1] a range summary is an estimate with low and high, is an answer's outcome, and no figure reads it\n   371\t    outcome_ids = {a.get('outcome') for a in calc['answers']}\n   372\t    for f in figs.values():\n   373\t        if f.get('scenario') != 'range':\n   374\t            continue\n   375\t        readers = [g['id'] for g in figs.values() if f['id'] in refs(g)]\n   376\t        if f['kind'] != 'estimate' or 'low' not in f or 'high' not in f or f['id'] not in outcome_ids or readers:\n   377\t            errors.append(('C4', f'{f[\"id\"]}: a range summary must be an estimate with low and high that is an answer\\'s outcome and feeds no figure'\n   378\t                                 + (f' (read by {\", \".join(readers)})' if readers else '')))\n   379\t\n   380\t    # C3 part within whole, C4 one forecast per shared quantity (every path)\n   381\t    def reachable(start, stop=None):\n   382\t        stops = set(stop) if isinstance(stop, (set, list, tuple)) else {stop}\n   383\t        seen_ids, stack = set(), [start]\n   384\t        while stack:\n   385\t            fid = stack.pop()\n   386\t            if fid in seen_ids or fid not in figs:\n   387\t                continue\n   388\t            seen_ids.add(fid)\n   389\t            if fid not in stops:\n   390\t                stack.extend(refs(figs[fid]))\n   391\t        return seen_ids\n   392\t    scenarios = {f.get('scenario', 'base') for f in figs.values() if f['basis'] == 'forecast'} or {'base'}\n   393\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n   394\t        if rel['type'] != 'part_of' or rel['part'] not in outcomes or rel['whole'] not in outcomes:\n   395\t            continue\n   396\t        part_m, whole_m = members[rel['part']], members[rel['whole']]\n   397\t        for sc in scenarios:\n   398\t            for period in family.get('compare_periods', []):\n   399\t                def node(view_id, member):\n   400\t                    want = (member['what']['population'], member['what']['measure'], member['what']['scope'], period)\n   401\t                    hits = [figs[f] for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id]) if _key(figs[f]['what']) == want\n   402\t                            and figs[f]['basis'] == 'forecast' and figs[f].get('scenario', 'base') == sc]\n   403\t                    return hits[0] if hits else None\n   404\t                p, w = node(rel['part'], part_m), node(rel['whole'], whole_m)\n   405\t                if p and w:\n   406\t                    (plo, phi), (wlo, whi) = _interval(p), _interval(w)\n   407\t                    if plo > wlo + 1e-9 or phi > whi + 1e-9:\n   408\t                        errors.append(('C3', f'{period} {sc}: {rel[\"part\"]} {p[\"id\"]} ({plo}–{phi}) exceeds {rel[\"whole\"]} {w[\"id\"]} ({wlo}–{whi})'))\n   409\t    for shared in family.get('shared', []):\n   410\t        want = _key(shared)\n   411\t        nodes = [f for f in figs.values() if _key(f['what']) == want and f['basis'] == 'forecast']\n   412\t        touched = [v for v, o in outcomes.items() if any(_key(figs[f]['what']) == want for f in reachable(o))]\n   413\t        if not touched:\n   414\t            continue\n   415\t        per_scenario = {}\n   416\t        for n in nodes:\n   417\t            per_scenario.setdefault(n.get('scenario', 'base'), []).append(n['id'])\n   418\t        if not nodes:\n   419\t            errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: no forecast node, though {\", \".join(touched)} depend on it'))\n   420\t        for sc, ids in sorted(per_scenario.items()):\n   421\t            if len(ids) != 1:\n   422\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want} {sc}: {len(ids)} forecast nodes ({\", \".join(ids)}); exactly one per scenario is required'))\n   423\t        stop = {n['id'] for n in nodes}\n   424\t        for f in figs.values():                       # [46i.1] scenario membership is derived along the whole path, not declared\n   425\t            sc = f.get('scenario', 'base')\n   426\t            if sc == 'range' or f['kind'] not in ('computed', 'estimate'):\n   427\t                continue\n   428\t            upstream = _upstream_of(f['id'], figs, refs)\n   429\t            borrowed = sorted(r for r in upstream if r in stop and figs[r].get('scenario', 'base') != sc)\n   430\t            if borrowed:\n   431\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {f[\"id\"]} ({sc}) depends on {\", \".join(borrowed)} of another scenario'))\n   432\t        for view_id in touched:                      # [46g.3] a bypass reaches the quantity through no forecast node of any scenario\n   433\t            bypass = [f for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id], stop=stop) if f not in stop and _key(figs[f]['what']) == want]\n   434\t            if bypass:\n   435\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {view_id} reaches {\", \".join(sorted(bypass))} without passing a forecast node ({\", \".join(sorted(stop))})'))\n   436\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):           # [46j.2] the later member rests on the earlier member's forecast nodes, per scenario\n   437\t        if rel['type'] != 'same_base' or rel['later'] not in outcomes or rel['earlier'] not in outcomes:\n   438\t            continue\n   439\t        base_key = _key(members[rel['earlier']]['what'])\n   440\t        earlier_graph = _upstream_of(outcomes[rel['earlier']], figs, refs) | {outcomes[rel['earlier']]}\n   441\t        earlier_nodes = {f for f in earlier_graph if _key(figs[f]['what']) == base_key and figs[f]['basis'] == 'forecast'}\n   442\t        reached = reachable(outcomes[rel['later']], stop=earlier_nodes)\n   443\t        bypass = [f for f in reached if f not in earlier_nodes and _key(figs[f]['what']) == base_key]\n   444\t        if not reached & earlier_nodes:\n   445\t            errors.append(('C9', f'{rel[\"later\"]} does not rest on {rel[\"earlier\"]}\\'s forecast ({\", \".join(sorted(earlier_nodes))})'))\n   446\t        if bypass:\n   447\t            errors.append(('C9', f'{rel[\"later\"]} reaches {\", \".join(sorted(bypass))} for {base_key} without {rel[\"earlier\"]}\\'s forecast'))\n   448\t    supplied = family.get('prior_answers', {})\n   449\t    for fig in figs.values():\n   450\t        earlier = fig['kind'] == 'prior' or fig.get('basis') == 'prior_forecast' or 'pointer' in fig   # [46i.2] derived, not labelled\n   451\t        if not earlier:\n   452\t            continue\n   453\t        if fig['kind'] != 'prior' or fig.get('basis') != 'prior_forecast':\n   454\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: an earlier forecast must be kind prior with basis prior_forecast'))\n   455\t        ptr, ans_prior = fig.get('pointer', {}), supplied.get(fig.get('pointer', {}).get('view'), {})\n   456\t        if ans_prior.get('day') != ptr.get('day') or not any(_same(fig.get('value'), v) for v in ans_prior.get('values', [])):\n   457\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: no earlier answer of {ptr.get(\"view\")} on {ptr.get(\"day\")} shown in the request states {fig.get(\"value\")}'))\n   458\t        owners = [a['view_id'] for a in calc['answers'] if a.get('outcome') == fig['id']]\n   459\t        if owners:                                    # [46h.2] nor the current outcome\n   460\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: an earlier forecast cannot be the current outcome of {\", \".join(owners)}'))\n   461\t        users = [f['id'] for f in figs.values() if fig['id'] in refs(f)]\n   462\t        if users:\n   463\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: an earlier forecast is for comparison only and cannot feed {\", \".join(users)}'))\n   464\t\n   465\t    recorded += _assumptions(family, figs, outcomes, calc, refs)\n   466\t    return {'errors': errors, 'recorded': recorded}\n   467\t\n   468\t\n   469\tdef _per_unit(op, ins, fig):\n   470\t    \"\"\"The per-unit identity: ratio(total, price per unit) -> units, product(units, price per unit) -> total, for one population and\n   471\t    scope. Labels are the judge's; a reader checks them against the passages.\"\"\"\n   472\t    out = fig['what']\n   473\t    if len(ins) != 2:\n   474\t        return False\n   475\t    same = all((i['what']['population'], i['what']['scope']) == (out['population'], out['scope']) for i in ins)\n   476\t    price = [i for i in ins if i['what']['measure'] == 'price per unit' and i['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')]\n   477\t    if op == 'ratio':\n   478\t        return same and len(price) == 1 and ins[1] is price[0] and out['measure'] == 'units' and ins[0]['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')\n   479\t    units = [i for i in ins if i['what']['measure'] == 'units' and i['unit'] == 'units']\n   480\t    return same and len(price) == 1 and len(units) == 1 and fig['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')\n   481\t\n   482\t\n   483\tdef changed(previous, answer, figs):\n   484\t    \"\"\"D728: whether a member's conclusion changed, derived by code from its earlier rung, outcome and source figures.\"\"\"\n   485\t    if previous is None:\n   486\t        return True, 'first judgement'\n   487\t    out = figs[answer['outcome']]\n   488\t    mid = sum(_interval(out)) / 2\n   489\t    sources = sorted(f['evidence'] + ':' + f['expression'] for f in figs.values() if f['kind'] == 'source')\n   490\t    reasons = []\n   491\t    if answer['rung'] != previous['rung']:\n   492\t        reasons.append(f'rung {previous[\"rung\"]} to {answer[\"rung\"]}')\n   493\t    if abs(mid - previous['outcome']) > 0.005 * max(abs(previous['outcome']), 1e-9):\n   494\t        reasons.append(f'outcome {previous[\"outcome\"]} to {round(mid, 3)}')\n   495\t    added, dropped = sorted(set(sources) - set(previous['sources'])), sorted(set(previous['sources']) - set(sources))\n   496\t    if added or dropped:\n   497\t        reasons.append(f'source figures added {added}, dropped {dropped}')\n   498\t    return bool(reasons), '; '.join(reasons) or 'unchanged'\n   499\t\n   500\t\n   275\tdef codes(result):\n   276\t    return {code for code, _ in result['errors']}\n   277\t\n   278\t\n   279\tMANIFEST = {}\n   280\t\n   281\t\n   282\tdef run():\n   283\t    rows = []\n   284\t\n   285\t    def item(name, family, passages, calc, ok, why):\n   286\t        MANIFEST[name] = {'family': family, 'calc': calc}\n   287\t        result = cc.check(family, passages, calc)\n   288\t        verdict, note = ok(result)\n   289\t        rows.append((name, verdict, note, result))\n   290\t\n   291\t    item('R1a', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1('a'),\n   292\t         lambda r: ('C3' in codes(r) and any('FY2027 Q4' in d for c, d in r['errors'] if c == 'C3'), 'C3 on Q4'), '')\n   293\t    item('R1b', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1('b'),\n   294\t         lambda r: ('C4' in codes(r) and 'C3' not in codes(r) and any('FY2027 Q3' in d and 'g3' in d for c, d in r['errors'] if c == 'C4'),\n   295\t                    'C4 on the Q3 bypass, no C3'), '')\n   296\t    item('R1c', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1('c'), lambda r: (not r['errors'], 'passes'), '')\n   297\t    item('R2', R2_FAMILY, R2_PASSAGES, r2(),\n   298\t         lambda r: (not r['errors'] and any(x['type'] == 'overlap' and x['figure'] == 'end' and abs(x['alternate'] - 35) < 0.01\n   299\t                                            and 50 in x['boundaries_crossed'] for x in r['recorded']), 'overlap recorded; ~35 crosses 50'), '')\n   300\t    item('R3a', R3_FAMILY, R3_PASSAGES, r3('a'),\n   301\t         lambda r: (any(c == 'C1' and 'a730' in d for c, d in r['errors']) and any(c == 'C1' and 'b800' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   302\t                    'C1 on both stripped qualifiers'), '')\n   303\t    item('R3b', R3_FAMILY, R3_PASSAGES, r3('b'),\n   304\t         lambda r: ('C1' not in codes(r) and 'C8' in codes(r), 'passes C1, C8 without bridges'), '')\n   305\t    item('R3c', R3_FAMILY, R3_PASSAGES, r3('c'),\n   306\t         lambda r: (not r['errors'] and sum(x['type'] == 'bridge' for x in r['recorded']) == 2, 'bridges recorded, undetermined'), '')\n   307\t    item('R4', R4_FAMILY, R4_PASSAGES, r4(),\n   308\t         lambda r: (not r['errors'] and any(x['type'] == 'adjustment' and x['figure'] == 'vera28' and 40 in x['boundaries_crossed']\n   309\t                                            and x['certainty'] == 'definite' for x in r['recorded']), 'trim definitely crosses 40'), '')\n   310\t    for name, maker in (('G1', g1), ('G2', g2), ('G3', g3), ('G4', g4)):\n   311\t        family, calc = maker()\n   312\t        item(name, family, G_PASSAGES, calc, lambda r: (not r['errors'], 'passes, estimates visible'), '')\n   313\t    f1, c1 = g1()\n   314\t    p1 = copy.deepcopy(c1)\n   315\t    p1['figures'][0]['value'] = 81.9\n   316\t    item('P1', f1, G_PASSAGES, p1, lambda r: (codes(r) == {'C1'} and any('gq1' in d for _, d in r['errors']), 'C1 only, on gq1'), '')\n   317\t    p2 = copy.deepcopy(c1)\n   318\t    gfy = next(f for f in p2['figures'] if f['id'] == 'gfy')\n   319\t    gfy['low'], gfy['high'] = 450.0, 480.0\n   320\t    item('P2', f1, G_PASSAGES, p2, lambda r: (codes(r) == {'C2'} and any('gfy' in d for _, d in r['errors']), 'C2 only, on gfy'), '')\n   321\t    p3a = copy.deepcopy(c1)\n   322\t    p3a['figures'].append({'id': 'pri', 'kind': 'prior', 'basis': 'prior_forecast', 'value': 425.0, 'unit': 'USD bn',\n   323\t                           'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'pointer': {'view': 'v1', 'day': '2026-07-13'}})\n   324\t    p3a['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'pri'}\n   325\t    f1p = dict(f1, prior_answers={'v1': {'day': '2026-07-13', 'values': [425.0]}})       # the earlier answer it points to, as shown\n   326\t    item('P3a', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3a, lambda r: (codes(r) == {'C5'}, 'C5 only'), '')\n   327\t    f2, c2 = g2()\n   328\t    g2x = copy.deepcopy(c2)\n   329\t    lo = next(f for f in g2x['figures'] if f['id'] == 'gdclo'); hi = next(f for f in g2x['figures'] if f['id'] == 'gdchi')\n   330\t    lo['inputs'], lo['value'] = ['gfyhi', 'gshlo'], 399.83                  # crossed: low share on the high total\n   331\t    hi['inputs'], hi['value'] = ['gfylo', 'gshhi'], 372.56\n   332\t    item('G2x', f2, G_PASSAGES, g2x, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']), 'C4: scenarios crossed'), '')\n   333\t    r1x = r1('b')\n   334\t    r1x['figures'].append(est('altq3', 108.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide as an alternate forecast', ['g3'],\n   335\t                              scenario='alt'))\n   336\t    next(f for f in r1x['figures'] if f['id'] == 'dcq3')['inputs'] = ['altq3', 'mix']\n   337\t    item('R1bx', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   338\t                                                         'C4: the base reads an alternate scenario'), '')\n   339\t    r1x2 = r1('b')                                    # routed through an intermediate segment figure\n   340\t    r1x2['figures'].append(est('altq3', 108.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide as an alternate forecast', ['g3'],\n   341\t                               scenario='alt'))\n   342\t    r1x2['figures'].append(comp('altdc', 'share', ['altq3', 'mix'], 99.9, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q3 interim'), scenario='alt'))\n   343\t    next(f for f in r1x2['figures'] if f['id'] == 'dcq3').update(operation='product', inputs=['altdc', 'one'], value=99.9)\n   344\t    r1x2['figures'].append({'id': 'one', 'kind': 'estimate', 'unit': 'x', 'basis': 'forecast', 'what': W('NVIDIA', 'factor', DC, 'FY2027 Q3'),\n   345\t                            'basis_text': 'unchanged', 'rests_on': [], 'value': 1.0})\n   346\t    item('R1bx2', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x2, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   347\t                                                           'C4: borrowed through an intermediate'), '')\n   348\t    r1x4 = r1('b')                                    # an alternate forecast computed from sources only (no estimate on its path)\n   349\t    r1x4['figures'].append(comp('altq3', 'sum', ['g3'], 108.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), relation='stated_in_addition',\n   350\t                                scenario='alt'))\n   351\t    next(f for f in r1x4['figures'] if f['id'] == 'dcq3')['inputs'] = ['altq3', 'mix']\n   352\t    item('R1bx4', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x4, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   353\t                                                           'C4: the base reads a source-only alternate forecast'), '')\n   354\t    r1x3 = r1('b')                                    # a point labelled range, read by the base\n   355\t    r1x3['figures'].append(est('altq3', 108.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide as a point', ['g3'], scenario='range'))\n   356\t    next(f for f in r1x3['figures'] if f['id'] == 'dcq3')['inputs'] = ['altq3', 'mix']\n   357\t    item('R1bx3', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x3, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'range summary' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   358\t                                                           'C4: a point labelled range'), '')\n   359\t    p3e2 = copy.deepcopy(p3a)                         # the earlier forecast relabelled as an estimate\n   360\t    pri = next(f for f in p3e2['figures'] if f['id'] == 'pri')\n   361\t    pri.update(kind='estimate', basis_text='our earlier figure', rests_on=[])\n   362\t    p3e2['answers'][0]['outcome'] = 'pri'\n   363\t    p3e2['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'gc392'}\n   364\t    item('P3e2', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3e2, lambda r: (any(c == 'C10' for c, d in r['errors']), 'C10: an earlier forecast relabelled'), '')\n   365\t    r1sc = r1('a')                                    # [46j.1] the company in base, Data Center in alt: the stored contradiction relabelled\n   366\t    for f in r1sc['figures']:\n   367\t        if f['id'] in ('dcq3', 'dcq4', 'dcfy'):\n   368\t            f['scenario'] = 'alt'\n   369\t    r1sc['figures'] = [f for f in r1sc['figures'] if f['id'] != 'prior414']\n   370\t    r1sc['answers'][1]['reference'] = {'unavailable': 'none supplied'}\n   371\t    item('R1sc', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1sc, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'cover' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   372\t                                                         'C4: part and whole in different scenarios'), '')\n   373\t    g2x2 = copy.deepcopy(c2)                          # [46j.1] crossing the non-shared share estimates\n   374\t    next(f for f in g2x2['figures'] if f['id'] == 'gdclo').update(inputs=['gfylo', 'gshhi'], value=372.56)\n   375\t    next(f for f in g2x2['figures'] if f['id'] == 'gdchi').update(inputs=['gfyhi', 'gshlo'], value=399.83)\n   376\t    item('G2x2', f2, G_PASSAGES, g2x2, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   377\t                                                   'C4: share estimates crossed'), '')\n   378\t    f24 = {'members': {'v1': V1, 'v22': {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2028'), 'bands': SEED['v22']}},\n   379\t           'relations': [{'type': 'same_base', 'later': 'v22', 'earlier': 'v1'}], 'shared': [W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027')],\n   380\t           'compare_periods': []}\n   381\t    c24 = copy.deepcopy(c2)                           # [46j.2] q22 on q01's published range, per scenario\n   382\t    c24['figures'] = [f for f in c24['figures'] if f['id'] not in ('gmix', 'gref2', 'gshlo', 'gshhi', 'gdclo', 'gdchi', 'gdc')] + [\n   383\t        src('g41', 'i090', '41%', 41.0, '%', 'consensus', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue growth', CO, 'FY2028')),\n   384\t        comp('g28lo', 'apply_growth', ['gfylo', 'g41'], 564.85, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2028'), scenario='low'),\n   385\t        comp('g28hi', 'apply_growth', ['gfyhi', 'g41'], 612.79, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2028'), scenario='high'),\n   386\t        est('g28', (560.0, 640.0), 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2028'), 'the two paths, widened for capex, Rubin pricing and Vera',\n   387\t            ['g28lo', 'g28hi', 'i256', 'i173'], scenario='range'),\n   388\t        src('gc554', 'i037', '$554 billion', 554.0, 'USD bn', 'consensus', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2028'))]\n   389\t    c24['answers'] = [ans('v1', 'gfy', 2, {'figure': 'gc392'}), ans('v22', 'g28', 2, {'figure': 'gc554'})]\n   390\t    item('G24', f24, G_PASSAGES, c24, lambda r: (not r['errors'], \"passes: q22 per scenario on q01's range\"), '')\n   391\t    prev = {'rung': 2, 'outcome': 417.5, 'sources': []}\n   392\t    calc_c = r1('c')\n   393\t    figs_c = {f['id']: f for f in calc_c['figures']}\n   394\t    prev['sources'] = sorted(f['evidence'] + ':' + f['expression'] for f in figs_c.values() if f['kind'] == 'source')\n   395\t    ch1 = cc.changed(dict(prev, outcome=418.4), calc_c['answers'][0], figs_c)\n   396\t    ch2 = cc.changed(dict(prev, rung=3, outcome=387.0), calc_c['answers'][0], figs_c)\n   397\t    rows.append(('CH1', ch1[0] is False, f'unchanged: {ch1[1]}', {'errors': [], 'recorded': []}))\n   398\t    rows.append(('CH2', ch2[0] is True and 'rung 3 to 2' in ch2[1], f'changed: {ch2[1]}', {'errors': [], 'recorded': []}))\n   399\t    p3e = copy.deepcopy(p3a)\n   400\t    p3e['answers'][0]['outcome'] = 'pri'\n   401\t    p3e['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'gc392'}\n   402\t    item('P3e', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3e, lambda r: (any(c == 'C10' and 'current outcome' in d for c, d in r['errors']), 'C10: a prior as the outcome'), '')\n   403\t    p3d = copy.deepcopy(p3a)\n   404\t    p3d['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'pri', 'unavailable': 'no consensus supplied'}\n   405\t    item('P3d', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3d, lambda r: (any(c == 'C5' and 'exactly one' in d for c, d in r['errors']), 'C5: both a figure and unavailable'), '')\n   406\t    p3c = copy.deepcopy(p3a)\n   407\t    next(f for f in p3c['figures'] if f['id'] == 'pri')['value'] = 431.0\n   408\t    item('P3c', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3c, lambda r: ('C10' in codes(r), 'C10: a prior figure the earlier answer does not state'), '')\n   409\t    p3b = copy.deepcopy(c1)\n   410\t    p3b['figures'].append(est('wrap', 425.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'our earlier forecast, close to the Street', ['gc392']))\n   411\t    p3b['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'wrap'}\n   412\t    item('P3b', f1, G_PASSAGES, p3b, lambda r: (codes(r) == {'C5'}, 'C5 only'), '')\n   413\t\n   414\t    f3, c3 = g3()\n   415\t    p4 = copy.deepcopy(c3)\n   416\t    next(f for f in p4['figures'] if f['id'] == 'gasp')['what']['scope'] = 'Rubin GPU'      # a price of another product\n   417\t    item('P4', f3, G_PASSAGES, p4, lambda r: (codes(r) == {'C8'} and any('gunits' in d for _, d in r['errors']),\n   418\t                                               'C8 only, on gunits: the per-unit identity needs one scope'), '')\n   419\t\n   420\t    g3inv = copy.deepcopy(c3)\n   421\t    g3inv['figures'].append(comp('gback', 'product', ['gunits', 'gasp'], 20.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Vera CPU', 'FY2027')))\n   422\t    item('G3inv', f3, G_PASSAGES, g3inv, lambda r: (not r['errors'], 'the per-unit inverse gives $20B'), '')\n   423\t    f4, c4 = g4()\n   424\t    g4m = copy.deepcopy(c4)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba render_v13.py | sed -n '29,152p'; cat judging-v13-draft.txt; rg -n 'D728' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba render_v13.py | sed -n '29,152p'; cat judging-v13-draft.txt; rg -n 'D728' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"    29\t\n    30\tdef v13_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\n    31\t    what = obj({k: S for k in ('population', 'measure', 'scope', 'period')},\n    32\t               'What the number measures: population, measure (the quantity, such as revenue or units; never its basis), scope, period.')\n    33\t    figure = obj({\n    34\t        'id': S, 'what': what,\n    35\t        'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.BASES - {'prior_forecast'}), 'description': 'reported: an actual; guidance: the company\\'s '\n    36\t                  'outlook; consensus: analysts\\' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this family\\'s forecast.'},\n    37\t        'scenario': S,\n    38\t        'kind': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['computed', 'estimate', 'source'], 'description': 'source: stated in a shown passage; computed: one '\n    39\t                 'operation on named figures; estimate: your judgement, stated as yours.'},\n    40\t        'value': nullable(N), 'low': nullable(N), 'high': nullable(N),\n    41\t        'bound': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['>', '>=', '<', '<=', 'approx', 'approx_below', 'approx_above']}),\n    42\t        'unit': S,\n    43\t        'evidence': nullable(S),\n    44\t        'expression': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Source only: the complete numeric expression exactly as the passage writes '\n    45\t                                'it, qualifiers included (for example \"more than $2 billion\", \"$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%\", \"more than triple\").'}),\n    46\t        'component': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['value', 'bound', 'midpoint', 'relative', 'low', 'high', 'multiplier']}),\n    47\t        'inputs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    48\t        'operation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.OPERATIONS)}),\n    49\t        'signs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': N}),\n    50\t        'relation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['time_aggregation', 'accounting_parts', 'stated_in_addition', 'overlap_unknown'],\n    51\t                              'description': 'Sum and roll_forward: periods of one quantity; declared parts of a whole; a source says they add; '\n    52\t                              'unknown overlap (name the disputed figure).'}),\n    53\t        'disputed': nullable(S),\n    54\t        'bridge': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Only when no listed identity covers the operation (periods of one quantity, '\n    55\t                            'declared parts, a balance and its flows, a stated share or multiplier, a total over a per-unit price): an '\n    56\t                            'estimate stating the conversion and listing the operands it converts.'}),\n    57\t        'basis_text': nullable(S), 'rests_on': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    58\t        'adjusts': nullable(obj({'figure': S, 'type': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['discount', 'uplift', 'trim']}})),\n    59\t        'converts': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    60\t    })\n    61\t    push = obj({'evidence_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    62\t    theme_push = obj({'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': theme_ids or ['none']},\n    63\t                      'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    64\t    answer = obj({\n    65\t        'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': member_ids},\n    66\t        'shape': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['forecast', 'unresolved']},\n    67\t        'outcome': nullable(S), 'rung': nullable({'type': 'integer'}),\n    68\t        'reference': nullable(obj({'figure': nullable(S), 'unavailable': nullable(S)}, 'An external figure, or a calculation from external '\n    69\t                              'and reported figures, or unavailable with why.')),\n    70\t        'reasons': S, 'why': nullable(S),\n    71\t        'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}},\n    72\t        'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': push}, 'theme_pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': theme_push},\n    73\t    })\n    74\t    return obj({'figures': {'type': 'array', 'items': figure}, 'answers': {'type': 'array', 'items': answer}})\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef parts(user):\n    78\t    head, rest = user.split('\\n\\n[Evidence in view', 1)\n    79\t    evidence = '[Evidence in view' + rest.split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0]\n    80\t    tail = '\\n\\n[' + rest.split('\\n\\n[', 1)[1] if '\\n\\n[' in rest else ''\n    81\t    blocks = {b.split(']', 1)[0]: '[' + b for b in tail.split('\\n\\n[')[1:]}\n    82\t    return head, evidence, blocks\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\tdef render(archive_path, calls, family):\n    86\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{archive_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    87\t    heads, lines, seen, themes, earlier = [], [], set(), '', []\n    88\t    for view_id, call_id in calls:\n    89\t        user = json.loads(archive.execute('select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?', (call_id,)).fetchone()[0])['messages'][1]['content']\n    90\t        head, evidence, blocks = parts(user)\n    91\t        heads.append(head)\n    92\t        for item in evidence.split('\\n- ')[1:]:\n    93\t            eid = item.split(' ', 1)[0]\n    94\t            if eid not in seen:\n    95\t                seen.add(eid)\n    96\t                lines.append('- ' + item)\n    97\t        themes = themes or next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Themes')), '')\n    98\t        prev = next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Previous')), '').split('\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema')[0]   # [46g.1] v7's output line goes\n    99\t        earlier.append(f'- {view_id}: ' + prev.replace('[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]', 'our earlier forecast, not a source:').strip())\n   100\t    rel = '; '.join(f'{r[\"part\"]} is part of {r[\"whole\"]}' for r in family['relations'] if r['type'] == 'part_of')\n   101\t    shared = '; '.join(f'{w[\"population\"]}, {w[\"measure\"]}, {w[\"scope\"]}, {w[\"period\"]}' for w in family['shared'])\n   102\t    user = ('[Family] members:\\n' + '\\n\\n'.join(heads) + f'\\n\\nRelations: {rel}.\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: {shared}.\\n\\n'\n   103\t            f'[Evidence in view for the family, {len(lines)} items]\\n' + '\\n'.join(lines) + '\\n\\n' + themes\n   104\t            + '\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.')   # D728: no earlier forecast\n   105\t    return user, sorted(seen), [t.split(' ', 1)[0] for t in themes.split('\\n- ')[1:]]\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tdef strict(calc, schema):\n   109\t    \"\"\"Fill every optional field with null, as strict structured output returns it.\"\"\"\n   110\t    fprops = schema['properties']['figures']['items']['properties']\n   111\t    aprops = schema['properties']['answers']['items']['properties']\n   112\t    figs = [{k: f.get(k) for k in fprops} for f in calc['figures']]\n   113\t    for f in figs:\n   114\t        f['scenario'] = f['scenario'] or 'base'\n   115\t        if f['what'] is None:\n   116\t            f['what'] = {'population': '', 'measure': '', 'scope': '', 'period': ''}\n   117\t    answers = []\n   118\t    for a in calc['answers']:\n   119\t        a2 = {k: a.get(k) for k in aprops}\n   120\t        if a2['reference'] is not None:\n   121\t            a2['reference'] = {'figure': a['reference'].get('figure'), 'unavailable': a['reference'].get('unavailable')}\n   122\t        a2['why'] = a.get('why')\n   123\t        answers.append(a2)\n   124\t    return {'figures': figs, 'answers': answers}\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\tdef without_nulls(calc):\n   128\t    clean = lambda d: {k: v for k, v in d.items() if v is not None}\n   129\t    answers = []\n   130\t    for a in calc['answers']:\n   131\t        a2 = clean(a)\n   132\t        if 'reference' in a2:\n   133\t            a2['reference'] = clean(a2['reference'])\n   134\t        answers.append(a2)\n   135\t    return {'figures': [clean(f) for f in calc['figures']], 'answers': answers}\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\tdef main():\n   139\t    archive = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite'\n   140\t    system = (HERE / 'judging-v13-draft.txt').read_text()\n   141\t    user, evidence_ids, theme_ids = render(archive, [('v14', 8729), ('v9', 8737)], gate.R1_FAMILY)\n   142\t    schema = v13_schema(['v14', 'v9'], evidence_ids, theme_ids)\n   143\t    calc = gate.r1('c')\n   144\t    answer = strict(calc, schema)\n   145\t    schema_errors = model.check_schema(answer, schema)\n   146\t    for a in answer['answers']:\n   147\t        a['cites'] = [e for e in a['cites'] if e in evidence_ids]\n   148\t    result = cc.check(gate.R1_FAMILY, gate.R1_PASSAGES, without_nulls(answer))\n   149\t    missing = sorted({f['evidence'] for f in calc['figures'] if f.get('evidence')} - set(evidence_ids))\n   150\t    report = [f'system {len(system)} characters; user {len(user)} characters; schema {len(json.dumps(schema))} characters',\n   151\t              f'evidence items {len(evidence_ids)}; themes {len(theme_ids)}',\n   152\t              f'source passages the answer cites that the rendered request does not show: {missing or \"none\"}',\nYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n\n- Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\n- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast per scenario. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n- \"Themes in force\" lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on a member and report it in that member's theme_pushes with the direction it pushes that member (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \"updated since this thesis was last judged\" may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n- Your conclusions must be consistent with each other and with the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open.\n- Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge rather than read or compute is an estimate, stated as yours. When the evidence cannot support a member's forecast, answer it unresolved and say why. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n11041:## D728 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the family judge does not see its earlier forecasts while calculating\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
