arios ['alt', 'base'] but v14 covers ['base']; related members cover the same\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'): dcq3 (base) depends on altq3 of another scenario\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'): dcfy (base) depends on altq3 of another scenario\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  R1bx2  C4: borrowed through an intermediate\n        C4: dcq3 (base) rests on estimates of another scenario (alt)\n        C4: dcfy (base) rests on estimates of another scenario (alt)\n        C4: v9 covers scenarios ['alt', 'base'] but v14 covers ['base']; related members cover the same\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'): dcq3 (base) depends on altq3 of another scenario\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'): dcfy (base) depends on altq3 of another scenario\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  R1bx4  C4: the base reads a source-only alternate forecast\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'): dcq3 (base) depends on altq3 of another scenario\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'): dcfy (base) depends on altq3 of another scenario\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  R1bx3  C4: a point labelled range\n        C4: altq3: a range summary must be an estimate with low and high that is an answer's outcome and feeds no figure (read by dcq3)\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'): dcq3 (base) depends on altq3 of another scenario\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'): dcfy (base) depends on altq3 of another scenario\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  P3e2   C10: an earlier forecast relabelled\n        C10: pri: an earlier forecast must be kind prior with basis prior_forecast\n        C10: pri: an earlier forecast cannot be the current outcome of v1\nPASS  R1sc   C4: part and whole in different scenarios\n        C4: v9 covers scenarios ['alt'] but v14 covers ['base']; related members cover the same\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'): v9 reaches g3 without passing a forecast node (q3f)\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  G2x2   C4: share estimates crossed\n        C4: gdclo (low) rests on estimates of another scenario (high)\n        C4: gdchi (high) rests on estimates of another scenario (low)\nPASS  G24    passes: q22 per scenario on q01's range\nPASS  CH1    unchanged: unchanged\nPASS  CH2    changed: rung 3 to 2; outcome 387.0 to 418.4\nPASS  P3e    C10: a prior as the outcome\n        C10: pri: an earlier forecast cannot be the current outcome of v1\nPASS  P3d    C5: both a figure and unavailable\n        C5: v1: the reference must name exactly one of a figure or unavailable\nPASS  P3c    C10: a prior figure the earlier answer does not state\n        C5: v1: the reference pri rests on the system's own forecast or an estimate\n        C10: pri: no earlier answer of v1 on 2026-07-13 shown in the request states 431.0\nPASS  P3b    C5 only\n        C5: v1: the reference wrap rests on the system's own forecast or an estimate\nPASS  P4     C8 only, on gunits: the per-unit identity needs one scope\n        C8: gunits: converts gt20, gasp to NVIDIA Vera CPU FY2027 units with no bridge naming those operands\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"adjustment\", \"figure\": \"gvera\", \"outcome\": \"v19\", \"value\": 13.0, \"alternate\": 20.0, \"alternate_bound\": null, \"boundaries_crossed\": [20], \"certainty\": \"definite\"}\nPASS  G3inv  the per-unit inverse gives $20B\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"adjustment\", \"figure\": \"gvera\", \"outcome\": \"v19\", \"value\": 13.0, \"alternate\": 20.0, \"alternate_bound\": null, \"boundaries_crossed\": [20], \"certainty\": \"definite\"}\nPASS  G4m    C9: FY2028 rests on consensus, not q01's forecast\n        C9: v22 does not rest on v1's forecast (gfy)\n        C9: v22 reaches gc392 for ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027') without v1's forecast\nPASS  R4m    C2: the bound direction reversed\n        C2: cpu28: its inputs make it a lower bound, but it is declared <\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"adjustment\", \"figure\": \"vera28\", \"outcome\": \"v41\", \"value\": 38.5, \"alternate\": 40.0, \"alternate_bound\": \"<\", \"boundaries_crossed\": [40], \"certainty\": \"possible\"}\nPASS  T1     accepted\nPASS  T2     accepted\nPASS  T3a    accepted\nPASS  T3b    accepted\nPASS  T4     accepted\nPASS  T5a    refused\n        C1: t: \"$730 billion\" is not a complete numeric expression of e1786\nPASS  T5b    refused\n        C1: t: \"$800 billion\" is not a complete numeric expression of e2535\nPASS  T6     refused\n        C1: t: \"double\" is not a complete numeric expression of e3660\nPASS  T7     refused\n        C1: t: value 108.5 USD bn bound None does not equal \"$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\" as component midpoint\nPASS  T8     refused\n        C1: t: value 730.0 USD bn bound None does not equal \"more than $730 billion\" as component value\nPASS  T9     refused\n        C1: t: \"$800 billion\" is not a complete numeric expression of e2535\nPASS  U1     decision held\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  U2     two refusals give unresolved\n        C2: gfy: declared 450.0–480.0 but sum of ['gh1', 'gh2'] gives 400.60–434.60\n\n47 items, 47 pass, misses: none\nGATE PASS\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
