{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '11032,11085p' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '102,143p'; nl -ba REQUEST-AUDIT.md | sed -n '57,86p'\"","aggregated_output":"- **Open after round 46j** (`codex-r46j.md`):\n  1. scenario names can still separate a part from its whole; related outcomes must cover the same scenarios;\n  2. the range rule refuses q22's reuse of q01's range; C9 must work per scenario;\n  3. an earlier forecast restated as a fresh estimate is invisible to code.\n\n  Codex proposes leaving the earlier forecasts out of the calculation request and comparing after. That changes what the judge sees\n  (D198: the previous conclusion carries the pieces not shown), so it goes to Alex.\n- **Not done:** nothing sent; no product file changed; the paid gate not asked.\n\n## D728 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the family judge does not see its earlier forecasts while calculating\n\n- **The question** (after D727): \"新判官算数的时候，要不要让它看到自己上一次的预测？… 不给看的代价：以前靠'上次结论'带着的那些老证据（这次没展示的）就丢了，只剩最近被引用过的和新到的证据。\"\n  Options:\n  - 算的时候不给看 (recommended: compute from the evidence alone, then compare with the earlier conclusion; the old pieces' carried\n    effect is lost and is measured in the paid test);\n  - 照旧给看.\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"算的时候不给看 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex), for judging-v13:**\n  - the calculation request shows no earlier forecast;\n  - whether a member's conclusion changed is derived by code afterwards, from its earlier rung, outcome and source figures;\n  - the evidence in view stays D198's arrivals and basis.\n- **D198 for judging-v7 is unchanged.**\n   102\t\n   103\t**Value × reader.**\n   104\t- **The calculation, the recorded assumptions and band-deciding flags:** read by the checks, the readers' packets, and later the\n   105\t  page.\n   106\t- **`unresolved`:** read by the round (no member updated) and the bundle (\"Forecast unavailable\", D726).\n   107\t- **The family declaration:** read by the request builder, C3, C4 and C7.\n   108\t- **Nothing in poc-v118 reads any of it.**\n   109\t\n   110\t**New path × old checks.**\n   111\t- v7's id, push and theme checks apply per member answer. Rung checks apply to `forecast` answers only [46b.5]. `cites` names shown\n   112\t  evidence only.\n   113\t- `cites_views` is always empty.\n   114\t- v7's request bytes are unchanged (the frozen pins).\n   115\t\n   116\t**State × event (the test harness).** Inputs are fixed: the stored requests' passages and the gold packet's items, as of the stored\n   117\tday.\n   118\t\n   119\t| Event | Outcome |\n   120\t|---|---|\n   121\t| success | the calculation and answers are recorded with their check results |\n   122\t| refusal | the errors are recorded; one retry with them |\n   123\t| second refusal | the family is unresolved, recorded |\n   124\t| a member's own `unresolved` [46b.5] | recorded; the family is held (no member updated) when any other member's outcome depends on a shared quantity or relation involving it; otherwise the others publish if they pass |\n   125\t| crash midway | the attempt is recorded incomplete and counts as no result |\n   126\t\n   127\tNothing writes a product store. Production lifecycle (members closing or opening, families changing) is designed only if the test\n   128\tpasses.\n   129\t\n   130\t**Prior decisions:**\n   131\t- D24, D28: bounded to the figures open questions consume.\n   132\t- D198: evidence in view, unioned.\n   133\t- D260, D263: the standard kept.\n   134\t- D359, D723: no product launcher.\n   135\t- D695: number questions.\n   136\t- D711, D721, D722: linking passed conclusions, and unresolved inclusion is not double counting.\n   137\t- D725, D726.\n   138\t\n   139\t## 5. The v13 request text (written and audited at $0 before the gate closes) [46.6]\n   140\t\n   141\t- **The basis:** judging-v7's standard sentences are kept, among them the reference, run-rate, discount, sizing, identities and\n   142\t  consistency.\n   143\t- **Replaced where they conflict with a family:**\n    57\t    why. It is never our earlier forecast.\n    58\t  - **unresolved:** why.\n    59\t\n    60\t## The family header (user message, before the evidence)\n    61\t\n    62\t`[Family] members: <id> (<question>, ladder …) …`, then:\n    63\t- `Relations: <part> is part of <whole>; <later> rests on <earlier>'s base.`\n    64\t- `Shared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: <population, measure, scope, period> …`\n    65\t\n    66\tThe family header, the members' earlier forecasts (labelled \"our earlier forecast, not a source\") and the union of evidence in view\n    67\tfollow the order of v7's request.\n    68\t\n    69\t## Earlier forecasts (D728, superseding the note below)\n    70\t\n    71\tThe calculation request shows no earlier forecast. The draft's first bullet now reads: judge every member from the evidence shown and\n    72\tthe themes in force, \"as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\"\n    73\tThe `changed` bullet and the answer fields `changed` and `why_changed` are removed, and code derives them. The schema offers no `prior`\n    74\tkind, no `prior_forecast` basis and no pointer. The system text is 4,373 characters.\n    75\t\n    76\t## Earlier forecasts [46f.4]\n    77\t\n    78\tThe draft says the earlier forecasts are \"supplied only for comparison\", and C10 makes that a check: a `prior` figure feeds no figure.\n    79\tThe design's earlier clause allowing a dated prior to feed a `same_base` is withdrawn. A later year reads the earlier member's forecast\n    80\tnode in the same call (C9).\n    81\t\n    82\t## Rendered and checked (`render_v13.py`, `render-r1.*`)\n    83\t\n    84\t- **The request:** the old-2 family on 09-20 (calls 8729 and 8737). System text 4,835 characters; user message 123,304 characters, with\n    85\t  237 evidence items, the family header, the themes once and the earlier forecasts labelled; schema 10,066 characters.\n    86\t- **The answer:** the R1c control answer, in strict shape (every optional field null). It passes `model.check_schema` with no error and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport pathlib,json,io,contextlib,copy,sys,types\nimport gate as g, calc_check as c, render_v13 as r, mutants\np=io.StringIO()\nwith contextlib.redirect_stdout(p):\n    result=g.main()\nassert result==0 and p.getvalue()==pathlib.Path('\\\\''gate-run7.txt'\\\\'').read_text()\nassert g.MANIFEST==json.loads(pathlib.Path('\\\\''gate-run7.fixtures.json'\\\\'').read_text())\np=io.StringIO()\nwith contextlib.redirect_stdout(p):\n    assert r.main()==0\nassert p.getvalue()==pathlib.Path('\\\\''render-r1.txt'\\\\'').read_text()\nreq=json.loads(pathlib.Path('\\\\''render-r1.request.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nprint('\\\\''run 7 log/manifest and render match, earlier heading present:'\\\\'', any(x in req['\\\\''user'\\\\''] for x in ('\\\\''[Earlier forecasts]'\\\\'','\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\'')))\noriginal=g.cc\npath=pathlib.Path('\\\\''calc_check.py'\\\\'')\nsrc=path.read_text()\nfor name,old,new,target in mutants.MUTANTS:\n    g.cc=original\n    if old:\n        assert src.count(old)==1,name\n        mod=types.ModuleType('\\\\''in_memory_calc_check'\\\\'')\n        exec(compile(src.replace(old,new),str(path),'\\\\''exec'\\\\''),mod.__dict__)\n        g.cc=mod\n    misses={name for name,ok,_,_ in g.run() if not ok}\n    assert (target in misses if target else not misses),(name,misses)\ng.cc=original\nprint('\\\\''reproduced'\\\\'',len(mutants.MUTANTS)-1,'\\\\''mutants'\\\\'')\ncase=copy.deepcopy(g.MANIFEST['\\\\''G24'\\\\''])\nfam,x=case['\\\\''family'\\\\''],case['\\\\''calc'\\\\'']\ndef fig(calc,fid):\n    return next(f for f in calc['\\\\''figures'\\\\''] if f['\\\\''id'\\\\'']==fid)\nf=fig(x,'\\\\''g28hi'\\\\'')\nf.clear()\nf.update(g.est('\\\\''g28hi'\\\\'',612.79,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'',g.W('\\\\''NVIDIA'\\\\'','\\\\''revenue'\\\\'',g.CO,'\\\\''FY2028'\\\\''),'\\\\''FY2028 capex and product mix independently put revenue here'\\\\'',['\\\\''i256'\\\\'','\\\\''i173'\\\\''],scenario='\\\\''high'\\\\''))\nsch=r.v13_schema(list(fam['\\\\''members'\\\\'']),list(g.G_PASSAGES),[])\nstrict=r.strict(x,sch)\nprint('\\\\''G24 without q01 high case:'\\\\'',r.model.check_schema(strict,sch),c.check(fam,g.G_PASSAGES,r.without_nulls(strict))['\\\\''errors'\\\\''])\nx=g.r1('\\\\''c'\\\\'')\nfigs={f['\\\\''id'\\\\'']:f for f in x['\\\\''figures'\\\\'']}\na=x['\\\\''answers'\\\\''][0]\nmember_deps=c._upstream_of(a['\\\\''outcome'\\\\''],figs,lambda f:f.get('\\\\''inputs'\\\\'',[])+[i for i in f.get('\\\\''rests_on'\\\\'',[]) if i in figs]+([f['\\\\''bridge'\\\\'']] if f.get('\\\\''bridge'\\\\'') else []))|{a['\\\\''reference'\\\\'']['\\\\''figure'\\\\'']}\nsources=sorted(f['\\\\''evidence'\\\\'']+'\\\\'':'\\\\''+f['\\\\''expression'\\\\''] for fid,f in figs.items() if f['\\\\''kind'\\\\'']=='\\\\''source'\\\\'' and fid in member_deps)\nprint('\\\\''CH1 with only v14 sources in the prior record:'\\\\'',c.changed({'\\\\''rung'\\\\'':2,'\\\\''outcome'\\\\'':418.4,'\\\\''sources'\\\\'':sources},a,figs))\narchive=r.REPO / '\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite'\\\\''\nf=copy.deepcopy(g.R1_FAMILY)\nf['\\\\''relations'\\\\'']=[{'\\\\''type'\\\\'':'\\\\''same_base'\\\\'','\\\\''earlier'\\\\'':'\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''later'\\\\'':'\\\\''v9'\\\\''}]\nu,_,_=r.render(archive,[('\\\\''v14'\\\\'',8729),('\\\\''v9'\\\\'',8737)],f)\nprint('\\\\''renderer with same_base declared:'\\\\'', next(x for x in u.splitlines() if x.startswith('\\\\''Relations:'\\\\'')))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
